      "content": "Suisse carries all human-facing copy: headlines, body, nav, buttons, card titles. Geist Mono appears the moment content becomes technical: code blocks, API examples, file names, URL strings, language switcher tabs. The split is binary — if a string could appear in a README, it should be mono. If it could appear in a brochure, it's Suisse. This binary creates a clear developer-first voice without needing additional visual cues."
